WEBVTT

00:03:29.747 --> 00:03:32.458
into the bounce of 
Josephine Baker’s banana dance.

00:03:32.541 --> 00:03:34.418
From jazz dance to jitterbug,

00:03:34.418 --> 00:03:36.629
from shake ya tailfeather
to shake your thang

00:03:36.629 --> 00:03:38.297
to that thang thangin.

00:03:38.297 --> 00:03:39.298
(Laughter)

00:03:39.507 --> 00:03:42.760
Black people carried
the origins of this dance through our DNA,

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:43.803
through our blood,

00:03:43.803 --> 00:03:44.887
through our bones.

00:03:44.971 --> 00:03:49.267
We made twerking the global,
cultural phenomenon it has become today.

00:03:49.934 --> 00:03:52.937
Now, as a big, Black woman who has ass,

00:03:52.937 --> 00:03:53.938
who can twerk

00:03:53.938 --> 00:03:55.815
and who’s been doing it her whole life,

00:03:55.815 --> 00:03:58.025
I kind of think I'm an expert
on the subject.

00:03:58.734 --> 00:04:03.364
I want to add to the classical etymology
of this dance because it matters.